    add();add('Every probability is an exact finite-population calculation over uniform 32-subsets of the same 1,932 valid N13 boards. The raw comparator is recomputed from the same joint distribution and exactly matches H3al’s previously published 32-positive probabilities. These are fixed inherited fits, not new optimizer runs. Expected capacity and exact graph recovery are descriptive. In bank 2, D4 exact graph recovery has probability 94.740109%, below its 96.044282% capacity-success probability.');add()
    add('**The intervention supplies a D4-invariance prior.** For each raw positive, it constructs the eight square rotations/reflections, deduplicates whole-board views, and deletes inherited finite displacement classes witnessed in those views. Only J/F entries belonging to witnessed inherited classes become zero; no other weights, unary terms, cardinality or source unit change. There is no optimizer refit, source completeness used as negative evidence, exposure recalibration, sparse-rule selection or target-dependent choice. Valid source labels, D4 invariance of the actual family and size-invariant translation-shared pair prohibitions are the assumptions supporting sound deletion. This does not establish validity for non-D4 rule families.');add()
    add('Each repair consumes **32 raw positive labels and 256 attempted deterministic views**, before deduplication. Those views are correlated and are not 256 independently labeled observations. Across the complete source population, 1,904 boards have eight unique D4 views, 24 have four and four have two. Three frozen source-only call fixtures produce 232, 232 and 244 unique views after batch deduplication; their counts are diagnostic examples, not an estimate of mean view cost. The 24 retained fixture calls cover all four fits and both arms using the same three draws.');add()
    add('The learner is a pure function accepting only the selected 32 positive boards, inherited F and finite offset list. It performs no file I/O, receives no population object and has no target-label or score argument. This is a function/interface separation, not a claim of operating-system process isolation. The distribution evaluator holds the complete source population and computes per-board raw/D4 joint masks only after the learner and protocol are hash-sealed. It checks all 169 coordinate basis cells against independent eight-map formulas, validates every transformed board using literal source queen/camel rules, and tests exact union factorization against concrete 32-board learner calls. Source statistics and full deletion outcomes are sealed before target scoring.');add()
    add('The exact distribution retains the joint outcome on the same raw draw: raw witness bits occupy the low half of each mask and augmented witness bits the high half. Integer Möbius inversion counts every selected 32-subset by its paired union. All **1,792 paired bank masks** remain in the evidence, including zero-mass outcomes; 80 mask-support records collapse only by equality of complete supports to **32 distinct graphs**. Positive-mass pairs number 16 for each of banks 0/1/3 and 48 for bank 2. Within-board, across-view and across-arm correlations are preserved, with no independence approximation. All four fits are retained.');add()
    add('The paired probability of raw success followed by D4 failure is exactly zero for every fit. D4 includes each original positive, so its deletion set contains the raw deletion set and its F is a subset of raw F. Before any capacity filtering, every possible repaired F is verified to contain true F. Consequently both arms have no invalid zero-F states, the complete 26,960-state true N15 census contains every repaired zero state, and filtering is complete. The exact key union over all 575 one/two/three-clue subsets uses the same previously examined 831,605 eligible H3aj inputs and exclusions. No new target cohort is created.');add()
    add('All decisions use rational integer comparisons: 20 ×covered ≥19 ×831605; 10 ×augmented favorable draws ≥9 ×total draws; and 10 ×(augmented favorable −raw favorable) ≥total draws. Large exact counts are stored as decimal strings. This is an exact conditional finite-population result, not a Monte Carlo confidence statement, independent training replication or untouched-test generalization result. The improvement concerns useful information obtained from a supplied symmetry prior at fixed raw-label count; it is not a wall-clock speedup claim.');add()
    add(f"The complete monitored stage used **{s['aggregate_CPU_seconds']:.6f} aggregate CPU seconds** and **{s['wall_seconds']:.6f} wall seconds**, within the frozen 120 CPU-second /180 wall-second envelope. It includes all transformation/distribution gates, source-label checks, joint statistics, pure-learner calls, support construction, completeness checks, all capacities and serialization. GPU work is zero. The independent publication audit took {s['audit']['elapsed_seconds']:.6f} additional wall seconds, including a full replay of the inherited H3al public evidence.");add()
    add('The independent audit reconstructs transformed boards with coordinate equations rather than numpy rotations, checks all transformed boards against the independently verified complete source census, rebuilds every raw/augmented joint mask, and matches every paired Möbius mass with a grouped binomial union dynamic program. It replays every concrete draw and view-count record, reconstructs all full supports, rebuilds all 32 integer clue histograms and packed flags, and recomputes every paired success category, expected capacity, exact graph probability and rational threshold.');add()
    add('H3i previously studied D4 augmentation with one bank draw, refitting and downstream search on a distinct conditioned evaluation set. H3am instead holds four inherited fits fixed, changes positive-witness deletion only and computes exact finite-population acquisition reliability on the seen H3aj universe. H3i’s search outcomes are not reused as evidence for this endpoint.');add()
